WEBVTT

00:01:22.967 --> 00:01:24.800
What the?!

00:03:12.633 --> 00:03:14.900
Okay, i think i found a way

00:03:14.934 --> 00:03:16.900
We can bypass that
construction just east of here.

00:03:16.934 --> 00:03:20.067
We might even make pennsylvania
faster than we thought.

00:03:20.101 --> 00:03:21.501
Yeah.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.800
Problem is we're not
going to pennsylvania.

00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:25.834
Wait... what?

00:03:25.867 --> 00:03:28.267
I just got a call from an old friend.

00:03:28.301 --> 00:03:30.267
Her father was killed last night.

00:03:30.301 --> 00:03:31.800
She thinks it might
be our kind of thing.

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:33.000
What?

00:03:33.034 --> 00:03:34.434
Yeah, believe me,

00:03:34.468 --> 00:03:37.934
<i>She never would've called,
never, if she didn't need us.</i>

00:03:39.967 --> 00:03:41.900
Come on. You coming or what?

00:03:53.134 --> 00:03:55.633
By "old friend," you mean...

00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:57.900
A friend that's not new.

00:03:57.934 --> 00:03:59.134
Yeah, thanks.

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:02.468
So, her name's cassie, huh?

00:04:02.501 --> 00:04:04.201
You never mentioned her.

00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:06.267
Didn't i? No.

00:04:06.301 --> 00:04:08.934
Yeah, we went out. You
mean you dated someone?

00:04:08.967 --> 00:04:12.234
For more than one night?

00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:14.900
Am i speaking a language
you're not getting here?

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:17.401
Dad and i were working
a job in athens, ohio.

00:04:17.434 --> 00:04:20.301
She was finishing up college.
We went out for a couple weeks.

00:04:20.334 --> 00:04:21.934
And?

00:04:25.234 --> 00:04:27.000
Look, it's terrible about her dad,

00:04:27.034 --> 00:04:29.667
But it kind of sounds like
a standard car accident.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.967
I'm not seeing how it
fits with what we do.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:35.201
Which, by the way, how
does she know what we do?

00:04:39.733 --> 00:04:42.667
You told her. You told her the secret.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:44.667
Our big family rule number one...

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:46.967
We do what we do and
we shut up about it.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:49.600
For a year and a half, i do
nothing but lie to jessica,

00:04:49.633 --> 00:04:52.301
And you go out with this
chick in ohio a couple of times

00:04:52.334 --> 00:04:54.568
And you tell her everything?

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:55.600
Dean!

00:04:55.633 --> 00:04:57.600
Yeah, looks like.

00:05:02.167 --> 00:05:04.234
Anderson: It's a
newspaper we put out here,

00:05:04.235 --> 00:05:06.067
Not a bulletin for the mayor's office.

00:05:06.101 --> 00:05:07.867
Get off your soapbox, jimmy.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:10.134
I'm urging a little discretion is all.

00:05:10.167 --> 00:05:13.234
No, i think you're telling
us what you want us to print

00:05:13.267 --> 00:05:15.167
And what you want us to sit on.

00:05:15.201 --> 00:05:16.967
I know you're upset, cassie.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.600
I liked your dad a lot.

00:05:18.633 --> 00:05:22.000
But i think your grief
is clouding your judgment.

00:05:22.034 --> 00:05:24.867
Two black people were killed
on the same stretch of road

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.667
In the same way in three weeks.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:28.468
Jimmy, you're too close to this.

00:05:28.501 --> 00:05:30.900
Those guys were friends of yours.

00:05:30.934 --> 00:05:36.301
Again, i'm very sorry for your loss.

00:05:45.733 --> 00:05:48.234
Dean.

00:05:48.267 --> 00:05:49.834
Hey, cassie.

00:05:55.934 --> 00:05:58.201
This is my brother, sam.

00:06:01.967 --> 00:06:03.568
I'm sorry about your dad.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:07.468
Yeah, me, too.

00:06:11.267 --> 00:06:14.101
My mother's in pretty bad shape.

00:06:14.134 --> 00:06:15.767
I've been staying with her.

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:18.267
I wish she wouldn't go off by herself.

00:06:18.301 --> 00:06:20.667
She's been snervous and frightened.

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:22.301
She was worried about dad.

00:06:22.334 --> 00:06:23.667
Why?

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:24.700
He was scared.

00:06:24.733 --> 00:06:26.267
He was seeing things.

00:06:26.301 --> 00:06:27.568
Like what?

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:30.468
He swore he saw an awful-Looking
black truck following him.

00:06:30.501 --> 00:06:32.867
A truck? Who was the driver?

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:35.900
He didn't talk about a
driver, just the truck.

00:06:35.934 --> 00:06:38.501
He said it would appear and disappear.

00:06:38.534 --> 00:06:41.367
And in the accident,
dad's truck was dented

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:44.501
Like it had been slammed
into by something big.

00:06:44.534 --> 00:06:45.733
Thanks.

00:06:45.767 --> 00:06:49.301
Now, you're sure this
dent wasn't there before?

00:06:49.334 --> 00:06:51.367
He sold cars, always drove a new one.

00:06:51.401 --> 00:06:53.468
There wasn't a scratch on that thing.

00:06:53.501 --> 00:06:57.301
It had rained hard that night.
There was mud everywhere.

00:06:57.334 --> 00:07:02.034
There was a distinct set of
muddy tracks from dad's car

00:07:02.067 --> 00:07:05.101
Leading right...

00:07:05.134 --> 00:07:08.101
To the edge where he went over.

00:07:09.501 --> 00:07:12.334
One set of tracks... his.

00:07:12.367 --> 00:07:15.034
And the first person killed
was a friend of your father's?

00:07:15.067 --> 00:07:16.468
Best friend... clayton solmes.

00:07:16.501 --> 00:07:18.201
They owned a car dealership together.

00:07:18.234 --> 00:07:22.101
Same thing... dent, no tracks.

00:07:22.134 --> 00:07:25.600
And the cops said exactly
what they said about dad...

00:07:25.633 --> 00:07:27.301
"He lost control of his car."

00:07:27.334 --> 00:07:29.534
Can you think of why your father
and partner might be targets?

00:07:29.568 --> 00:07:31.000
No.

00:07:31.034 --> 00:07:33.034
You think this vanishing
truck ran him off the road?

00:07:33.067 --> 00:07:36.767
When you say it aloud like that...

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:42.134
Listen, i'm a little skeptical
about this ghost stuff

00:07:42.167 --> 00:07:44.667
Or whatever it is you guys are into.

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:46.201
Skeptical.

00:07:46.234 --> 00:07:48.700
If i remember, i think
you said i was nuts.

00:07:48.733 --> 00:07:50.568
That was then.

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:52.867
Hmm.

00:07:54.867 --> 00:07:57.468
I just know that i can't
explain what happened up there,

00:07:57.501 --> 00:07:59.167
So i called you.

00:08:00.733 --> 00:08:03.468
Mom. Where have you been?

00:08:03.501 --> 00:08:07.534
I had no idea you'd
invited friends over.

00:08:07.568 --> 00:08:11.900
Mom, this is dean, a friend
of mine from... college,

00:08:11.934 --> 00:08:14.468
And his brother, sam.

00:08:14.501 --> 00:08:18.800
Well, l-L-L-I
won't interrupt you.

00:08:18.834 --> 00:08:20.067
Mrs. Robinson? Hmm?

00:08:20.101 --> 00:08:22.534
We're sorry for your loss.

00:08:22.568 --> 00:08:25.534
We'd like to talk to you for
a minute, if you don't mind.

00:08:25.568 --> 00:08:29.900
I'm really not up to that just now.

00:09:25.301 --> 00:09:27.900
Dd: Jimmy meant something to this town.

00:09:27.934 --> 00:09:29.633
He was one of our best.

00:09:29.667 --> 00:09:32.167
It won't be the same without him.

00:09:32.201 --> 00:09:35.134
Our best seem to be dropping like flies.

00:09:35.167 --> 00:09:37.000
Clayton, my father, jimmy.

00:09:37.034 --> 00:09:39.800
What is it exactly you want me to do?

00:09:39.834 --> 00:09:43.800
Well, how about closing this
section of road for starters?

00:09:43.834 --> 00:09:46.000
Close the main road, the
only road in and out of town?

00:09:46.034 --> 00:09:50.134
Accidents happen, cassie. That's
what they are... accidents.

00:09:50.167 --> 00:09:52.568
Did the cops check for
denting on jimmy's car

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:54.234
To see if it was pushed?

00:09:54.267 --> 00:09:55.434
Who's this?

00:09:55.468 --> 00:09:58.401
Dean and sam winchester, family friends.

00:09:58.434 --> 00:10:01.568
This is mayor harold todd.

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:04.767
There's one set of tracks...
one. Doesn't point to foul play.

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:07.101
Mayor, the police and town officials

00:10:07.134 --> 00:10:08.867
Take their cues from you...
if you're indifferent about...

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:10.167
Indifferent?

00:10:10.201 --> 00:10:13.034
Would you close the road
if the victims were white?

00:10:13.067 --> 00:10:15.867
You're suggesting i'm racist, cassie.

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:19.434
I'm the last person you
should talk to like that.

00:10:19.468 --> 00:10:20.434
Why is that?

00:10:20.468 --> 00:10:22.667
Why don't you k your mother?

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:31.534
I'll say this for her... she's fearless.

00:10:31.568 --> 00:10:32.600
Mm-Hmm.

00:10:32.633 --> 00:10:36.134
Bet she kicked your ass a coupleimes.

00:10:36.167 --> 00:10:39.800
What's interesting is you guys
never really look at each other

00:10:39.834 --> 00:10:40.934
At the same time.

00:10:40.967 --> 00:10:43.401
You look at her when she's not looking.

00:10:43.434 --> 00:10:45.834
She checks you out when you look away.

00:10:47.367 --> 00:10:51.201
It's just a... just an
interesting observation

00:10:51.234 --> 00:10:54.834
In a, you know,
observationally interesting way.

00:10:54.867 --> 00:10:57.568
You think we might have some
more pressing issues here?

00:10:57.600 --> 00:10:59.900
Hey, if i'm hitting a nerve...

00:10:59.934 --> 00:11:01.234
Oh, let's go.

00:11:16.201 --> 00:11:18.401
Excuse me. Are you ron stubbins?

00:11:18.434 --> 00:11:20.234
Friends with jimmy anderson?

00:11:20.267 --> 00:11:21.434
Who are you?

00:11:21.468 --> 00:11:24.067
We're with mr. Anderson's
insurance company.

00:11:24.101 --> 00:11:26.900
Just here to dot some
i's and cross some t's.

00:11:26.934 --> 00:11:29.201
We were just wondering,
had the deceased mentioned

00:11:29.234 --> 00:11:30.767
Any unusual recent experiences?

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:32.234
What do you mean, "unusual"?

00:11:32.267 --> 00:11:34.067
Well, visions, hallucinations.

00:11:34.101 --> 00:11:37.000
It's all part of a medical
examination kind of thing.

00:11:37.034 --> 00:11:39.101
What company you say you were with?

00:11:39.134 --> 00:11:41.434
All tional mutual.

00:11:41.468 --> 00:11:45.034
Tell me, did he ever
mention seeing a truck,

00:11:45.067 --> 00:11:47.034
A big black truck?

00:11:47.067 --> 00:11:49.434
What the hell you talking
about? You even speaking english?

00:11:49.468 --> 00:11:52.867
Son, this truck, a big,
scary, monster-Looking thing?

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:54.568
Yeah, actually, i think so.

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:56.633
Hmm.

00:11:56.667 --> 00:11:58.301
What?

00:11:58.334 --> 00:11:59.934
I have heard of a truck like that.

00:11:59.967 --> 00:12:01.234
You have?

00:12:01.267 --> 00:12:02.267
Where?

00:12:02.301 --> 00:12:04.434
Not where... when.

00:12:04.468 --> 00:12:07.800
Back in the '60s, there
was a string of deaths.

00:12:07.834 --> 00:12:10.201
Black men.

00:12:10.234 --> 00:12:14.534
Stores they disappeared in
a big, nasty black truck.

00:12:14.568 --> 00:12:16.067
They ever catch the guy who did it?

00:12:16.101 --> 00:12:17.134
Never found him.

00:12:17.167 --> 00:12:21.800
Hell, not sure they even really looked.

00:12:21.834 --> 00:12:24.000
See, there was a time

00:12:24.034 --> 00:12:30.867
This town wasn't too
friendly to all its citizens.

00:12:33.234 --> 00:12:34.301
Thank you.

00:12:39.101 --> 00:12:40.101
Truck.

00:12:40.134 --> 00:12:41.568
Keeps coming up, doesn't it?

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:43.834
<i>I was thinking. You heard
of the flying dutchman?</i>

00:12:43.867 --> 00:12:46.468
Yeah, a ghost ship infused
with the captain's evil spirit.

00:12:46.501 --> 00:12:48.034
It was basically a part of him.

00:12:48.067 --> 00:12:50.201
So, what if we're dealing
with the same thing?

00:12:50.234 --> 00:12:53.000
A phantom truck who's the
extension of some bastard ghost,

00:12:53.034 --> 00:12:54.201
Re-Enacting past crimes.

00:12:54.234 --> 00:12:56.067
The victims have all been black men.

00:12:56.101 --> 00:12:57.600
I think it's more than that.

00:12:57.633 --> 00:13:00.401
They all seem connected
to cassie and her family.

00:13:00.434 --> 00:13:02.600
All right, well, you work that angle.

00:13:02.633 --> 00:13:03.667
Go talk to her.

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:04.934
Yeah, i will.

00:13:04.967 --> 00:13:07.201
Oh, and you might also want
to mention that other thing.

00:13:07.234 --> 00:13:09.767
What other thing?

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:12.733
That serious unfinished business.

00:13:12.767 --> 00:13:16.367
Dean, what is going on between you two?

00:13:16.401 --> 00:13:18.834
So maybe we were a little
bit more involved than i said.

00:13:18.867 --> 00:13:21.834
Oh, okay, yeah.

00:13:21.867 --> 00:13:23.900
Okay, a lot more... maybe.

00:13:23.934 --> 00:13:27.034
I told her the secret about
what we do, and i shouldn't have.

00:13:27.067 --> 00:13:30.034
Look, man, everybody's got to
open up to someone sometime.

00:13:30.067 --> 00:13:31.334
Yeah, i don't.

00:13:31.367 --> 00:13:34.600
It was stupid to get that
close. I mean, look how it ended.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:37.600
Would you stop?

00:13:39.501 --> 00:13:41.468
Blink or something.

00:13:41.501 --> 00:13:43.067
You loved her.

00:13:43.101 --> 00:13:44.234
Oh, god.

00:13:44.267 --> 00:13:48.800
You were in love with
her, but you dumped her.

00:13:51.201 --> 00:13:53.767
Oh, wow.

00:13:55.501 --> 00:13:56.867
She dumped you.

00:13:56.900 --> 00:13:59.700
Get in the car.

00:13:59.733 --> 00:14:01.834
Get in the car!

00:14:17.034 --> 00:14:18.367
Dean.

00:14:18.401 --> 00:14:19.934
Hey. Hey.

00:14:19.967 --> 00:14:22.101
Come on in.

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:27.834
So, you busy?

00:14:27.867 --> 00:14:29.367
The paper is doing a tribute to jimmy.

00:14:29.401 --> 00:14:34.401
I was just going through
his stuff, his awards,

00:14:34.434 --> 00:14:37.334
Trying to find the words.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.167
That's got to be tough.

00:14:41.201 --> 00:14:43.600
For years this family owned
the paper, the dorians.

00:14:43.633 --> 00:14:45.600
They had a whites-Only staff policy.

00:14:45.633 --> 00:14:49.534
After they sold it, jimmy
became the first black reporter.

00:14:49.568 --> 00:14:52.401
He became editor.

00:14:52.434 --> 00:14:54.568
He taught me everything.

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:56.034
Where's your brother?

00:14:57.834 --> 00:14:59.134
Not here.

00:14:59.167 --> 00:15:01.334
All right, so, what brings you here?

00:15:01.367 --> 00:15:03.401
I'm trying to find the connection

00:15:03.434 --> 00:15:04.934
Between the three victims.

00:15:04.967 --> 00:15:06.434
By the way, did you talk to your mom

00:15:06.468 --> 00:15:08.501
About what todd said
about not being a racist?

00:15:08.534 --> 00:15:09.700
I did.

00:15:09.733 --> 00:15:13.000
She didn't want to talk about it.

00:15:15.534 --> 00:15:19.167
So, just then, why did you
ask where my brother was?

00:15:19.201 --> 00:15:20.600
Nothing. Not important.

00:15:20.633 --> 00:15:23.633
Could it be because without
him here it'just you and me

00:15:23.667 --> 00:15:25.501
And not you, me, and sam,
which would be easier?

00:15:25.534 --> 00:15:26.800
It's not easier.

00:15:26.834 --> 00:15:28.501
Look...

00:15:28.534 --> 00:15:31.234
No, forget it. It's fine.

00:15:31.267 --> 00:15:34.301
Keep it strictly business.

00:15:34.334 --> 00:15:36.800
I forgot you do that.

00:15:36.834 --> 00:15:39.367
Do what?

00:15:39.401 --> 00:15:41.767
Oh, whenever we get...

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:44.034
What's the word, close?...

00:15:44.067 --> 00:15:46.834
Anywhere in the neighborhood
of emotional vulnerability,

00:15:46.867 --> 00:15:49.267
You back off or make some joke

00:15:49.301 --> 00:15:51.301
Or find any way to shut the door on me.

00:15:51.334 --> 00:15:53.234
Oh, that's hilarious.

00:15:53.267 --> 00:15:56.034
See, i'm not the one who
took that big, final door

00:15:56.067 --> 00:15:57.867
And slammed it behind
me, and i'm not the one

00:15:57.900 --> 00:15:59.367
Who took the key and buried it.

00:15:59.401 --> 00:16:01.101
Are we done with this metaphor?

00:16:01.134 --> 00:16:02.733
All i'm saying is i was totally
up front with you back then

00:16:02.767 --> 00:16:03.800
And you nailed me with it.

00:16:03.834 --> 00:16:05.767
The guy i'm hoping might be in my future

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:07.700
Tells me he professionally pops ghosts.

00:16:07.733 --> 00:16:09.134
Those weren't the words i used.

00:16:09.167 --> 00:16:11.334
And he has to leave too
work with his father. I did.

00:16:11.367 --> 00:16:13.000
All i could think was,
if you want out, fine.

00:16:13.034 --> 00:16:14.967
But don't tell me this insane story.

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:16.401
It was the truth, cassie,

00:16:16.434 --> 00:16:18.900
It didn't sound so insane the
minute you thought i could help.

00:16:18.934 --> 00:16:21.000
Back then i thought you
just wanted to dump me.

00:16:21.034 --> 00:16:23.800
Whoa, let's not forget
who dumped who, okay?

00:16:23.834 --> 00:16:26.000
I thought it was what you wanted.

00:16:26.034 --> 00:16:27.134
Well, it wasn't.

00:16:27.167 --> 00:16:28.967
I didn't mean to hurt you.

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:29.967
Well, you did.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.934
I'm sorry. Yeah, me, too.

00:18:34.367 --> 00:18:37.000
Absolutely.

00:18:37.033 --> 00:18:40.033
Actually, we were always
pretty good at fighting.

00:18:40.067 --> 00:18:42.534
This, we were good at.

00:18:42.567 --> 00:18:46.900
It's all the other stuff, not so much.

00:18:46.933 --> 00:18:49.667
Hey, i tried.

00:18:49.701 --> 00:18:53.734
I told you who i really was.
It was a big first for me.

00:18:53.768 --> 00:18:55.933
Why'd you tell me?

00:18:55.967 --> 00:18:58.367
I don't know.

00:19:01.367 --> 00:19:04.701
I guess i couldn't lie to you.

00:19:07.501 --> 00:19:09.567
Dean...

00:19:09.601 --> 00:19:13.134
When you told me that story,

00:19:13.167 --> 00:19:14.933
It scared the hell out of me.

00:19:14.967 --> 00:19:19.300
I thought you were nuts, dangerous even.

00:19:19.334 --> 00:19:22.933
Actually...

00:19:22.967 --> 00:19:27.267
Maybe i was looking for
a reason to walk away.

00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:33.000
In my work i see some horrible things,

00:19:33.033 --> 00:19:35.768
Things that can't be explained.

00:19:35.801 --> 00:19:37.200
I deal with them.

00:19:37.234 --> 00:19:39.834
But working things out with you?

00:19:39.868 --> 00:19:42.501
I'm a scary one, all right.

00:19:42.534 --> 00:19:44.067
Hmm.

00:19:49.834 --> 00:19:54.434
Well, usually thgs get worked out

00:19:54.467 --> 00:19:57.234
When you really want them to.

00:20:01.534 --> 00:20:05.900
Yeah, but i'm still really
involved in my dad's work.

00:20:08.067 --> 00:20:13.601
No more excuses, okay? From you or me.

00:20:13.634 --> 00:20:14.834
Okay.

00:20:32.100 --> 00:20:34.900
Yeah

00:20:34.933 --> 00:20:38.033
You're kidding.

00:20:42.200 --> 00:20:43.768
And he's with me.

00:20:45.768 --> 00:20:48.033
Where were you last night?

00:20:48.067 --> 00:20:51.067
You didn't make it back to the motel.

00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:52.200
Nope.

00:20:52.234 --> 00:20:54.167
I'm guessing you guys worked things out.

00:20:54.200 --> 00:20:56.200
We'll be working things
out when we're 90.

00:20:56.234 --> 00:20:57.501
So, what happened?

00:20:57.534 --> 00:20:59.834
Every bone crushed, internal
organs turned to pudding.

00:20:59.868 --> 00:21:01.067
The cops are all stumped,

00:21:01.100 --> 00:21:02.967
But it's almost like
something ran him over.

00:21:03.000 --> 00:21:04.534
Something like a truck? Yep.

00:21:04.567 --> 00:21:06.634
Tracks? Nope.

00:21:06.667 --> 00:21:08.734
What was the mayor doing here anyway?

00:21:08.768 --> 00:21:11.200
He owned the property.
Bought it a few weeks ago.

00:21:11.234 --> 00:21:13.367
Yeah, but he's white.
Doesn't fit the pattern.

00:21:13.401 --> 00:21:15.234
Killings didn't happen up on the road.

00:21:15.267 --> 00:21:18.134
That doesn't fit, either.

00:21:24.067 --> 00:21:25.334
Thanks.

00:21:25.367 --> 00:21:27.701
I'm trying to find some
link between those killings

00:21:27.734 --> 00:21:29.501
In the '60s and what's going on now.

00:21:29.534 --> 00:21:31.467
There wasn't a lot
about it in the paper.

00:21:31.501 --> 00:21:34.334
Not surprising. Probably
minimal-Police-Work deal.

00:21:34.367 --> 00:21:36.667
Back then, equal justice under the law

00:21:36.701 --> 00:21:38.601
Wasn't too literal around here.

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:42.367
Yeah?

00:21:42.401 --> 00:21:43.933
Sam: Okay, the courthouse records

00:21:43.967 --> 00:21:47.100
Show that mr. And mrs. Mayor
bought an abandoned property.

00:21:47.134 --> 00:21:49.100
The previous owner
was the dorian family,

00:21:49.134 --> 00:21:50.534
For like 150 years.

00:21:50.567 --> 00:21:51.868
Dorian? Yeah.

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:54.300
Didn't you say the dorian
family used to own this paper?

00:21:54.334 --> 00:21:56.300
Along with most everything
else around here.

00:21:56.334 --> 00:21:58.467
Real pillars of the town.

00:21:58.501 --> 00:21:59.768
Right, right.

00:22:02.300 --> 00:22:03.734
That's interesting.

00:22:03.768 --> 00:22:05.701
What?

00:22:05.734 --> 00:22:08.801
This cyrus dorian, he
vanished in april of '63.

00:22:08.834 --> 00:22:11.801
The case was investigated
but never solved.

00:22:11.834 --> 00:22:14.167
It was the time the string
of murders was going on.

00:22:14.200 --> 00:22:15.868
Well, i pulled a bunch of
paper up on the dorian place.

00:22:15.900 --> 00:22:17.567
It must've been in bad shape
when the mayor bought it.

00:22:17.601 --> 00:22:19.100
Why is that?

00:22:19.134 --> 00:22:20.801
The first thing he did
was bulldoze the place.

00:22:20.834 --> 00:22:23.501
Mayor todd knocked down the dorianlace?

00:22:23.534 --> 00:22:27.200
It was a big deal. One of
the oldest local houses left.

00:22:27.234 --> 00:22:28.801
It made the front page.

00:22:28.834 --> 00:22:29.967
You got a date?

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:33.267
Uh... the 3rd of last month.

00:22:37.467 --> 00:22:40.933
Mayor todd bulldozed the
dorian family home on the 3rd.

00:22:40.967 --> 00:22:43.834
The first killing was the very next day.

00:24:06.300 --> 00:24:07.768
Dean!

00:24:11.980 --> 00:24:14.047
Maybe you could throw
a couple shots in that.

00:24:14.980 --> 00:24:18.714
You didn't see who
was driving the truck?

00:24:20.114 --> 00:24:21.514
It seemed to be no one.

00:24:24.413 --> 00:24:26.614
Everything was moving so fast.

00:24:28.317 --> 00:24:33.617
And then it was just gone.
Why didn't it kill us?

00:24:33.651 --> 00:24:37.317
Whatever is controlling the
truck wants you afraid first.

00:24:37.350 --> 00:24:42.517
Mrs. Robinson, cassie said
that your husband saw the truck

00:24:42.551 --> 00:24:45.183
Before he died.

00:24:45.217 --> 00:24:46.517
Mom?

00:24:46.551 --> 00:24:48.018
Hmm?

00:24:48.984 --> 00:24:51.851
Martin was under a lot of stress.

00:24:51.884 --> 00:24:53.851
You can't be sure about
what he was seeing.

00:24:53.884 --> 00:24:56.250
Well, after tonight i think
we can be reasonably sure

00:24:56.284 --> 00:24:57.651
That he was seeing a truck.

00:24:57.684 --> 00:25:02.984
What happened tonight, you
and cassie are marked, okay?

00:25:03.018 --> 00:25:05.350
Your daughter could die,
so if you know something,

00:25:05.384 --> 00:25:07.317
Now would be a really good
time to tell us about it.

00:25:07.350 --> 00:25:09.217
Dean... yes.

00:25:09.250 --> 00:25:11.918
Yes, he said he saw a truck.

00:25:11.951 --> 00:25:14.150
Did he know who it belonged to?

00:25:14.183 --> 00:25:16.484
He thought he did. Who was that?

00:25:18.551 --> 00:25:21.517
Cyrus...

00:25:21.551 --> 00:25:24.617
A man named cyrus.

00:25:27.951 --> 00:25:30.350
Is this cyrus?

00:25:30.384 --> 00:25:35.984
Cyrus dorian died
more than 40 years ago.

00:25:36.018 --> 00:25:40.284
How do you know he died, mrs. Robinson?

00:25:41.984 --> 00:25:44.183
The paper said he went missing.

00:25:44.217 --> 00:25:46.551
How do you know he died?

00:25:46.584 --> 00:25:50.217
We were all very young.

00:25:52.217 --> 00:25:55.083
I dated cyrus a while.

00:25:55.117 --> 00:25:58.183
I was also seeing martin,
in secret of course

00:25:58.217 --> 00:26:04.450
'Cause interracial couples
didn't go over too well then.

00:26:04.484 --> 00:26:06.984
When i broke it off with cyrus,

00:26:07.018 --> 00:26:09.918
And when he found out about martin...

00:26:09.951 --> 00:26:15.417
I don't know... he changed.

00:26:15.450 --> 00:26:21.250
His hatred... his
hatred was frightening.

00:26:21.284 --> 00:26:22.751
The string of murders.

00:26:22.784 --> 00:26:25.250
There were rumors,

00:26:25.284 --> 00:26:28.117
People of color disappearing
into some kind oa truck.

00:26:31.484 --> 00:26:34.217
Nothing was ever done.

00:26:39.517 --> 00:26:41.417
Martin and...

00:26:43.417 --> 00:26:47.717
Martin and i, we were gonna be married

00:26:47.751 --> 00:26:49.751
In that little church near here,

00:26:49.784 --> 00:26:52.684
But last minute, we decided to elope

00:26:52.717 --> 00:26:55.018
'Cause we didn't want all the attention.

00:26:55.050 --> 00:26:56.284
And cyrus?

00:27:03.018 --> 00:27:08.317
The day we set for the wedding

00:27:08.350 --> 00:27:13.884
Was the day someone
set fire to the church.

00:27:21.984 --> 00:27:27.183
There was a children's
choir practicing in there.

00:27:29.651 --> 00:27:32.784
They all died.

00:27:35.217 --> 00:27:37.784
Did the attacks stop after that?

00:27:37.817 --> 00:27:40.751
No, there was one more.

00:27:42.751 --> 00:27:47.551
One night that truck came for martin.

00:27:50.018 --> 00:27:52.484
Cyrus beat him something terrible,

00:27:57.183 --> 00:28:00.384
But martin... you see, martin got loose

00:28:00.417 --> 00:28:03.250
And he started hitting cyrus

00:28:03.284 --> 00:28:07.484
And he just kept hitting
him and hitting him.

00:28:18.751 --> 00:28:21.083
Why didn't you call the cops?

00:28:25.417 --> 00:28:28.617
This was 40 years ago.

00:28:28.651 --> 00:28:32.250
He called on his friends...

00:28:32.284 --> 00:28:34.217
Clayton, solmes, and jimmy anderson...

00:28:34.250 --> 00:28:37.584
And they put cyrus' body into the truck

00:28:37.617 --> 00:28:42.183
And then rolled it into the
swamp at the edge of his land

00:28:42.217 --> 00:28:48.717
And all three of them kept
that secret all these years.

00:28:50.751 --> 00:28:52.183
And now all three are gone.

00:28:52.217 --> 00:28:53.317
So is mayor todd.

00:28:55.083 --> 00:28:58.384
Now, he said that you of all people

00:28:58.417 --> 00:29:00.217
Would know that he is not a racist.

00:29:00.250 --> 00:29:01.284
Why would he say that?

00:29:01.317 --> 00:29:02.317
He was a good man.

00:29:02.350 --> 00:29:05.617
He was a young deputy back then,

00:29:05.651 --> 00:29:07.384
Investigating cyrus's disappearance.

00:29:07.417 --> 00:29:13.117
Once he figured out what
martin and the others had done,

00:29:13.150 --> 00:29:18.951
He he did nothing

00:29:20.617 --> 00:29:23.684
Because he also knew
what cyrus had done.

00:29:26.817 --> 00:29:28.484
Why didn't you tell me?

00:29:28.517 --> 00:29:31.183
I thought i was protecting them.

00:29:33.250 --> 00:29:38.350
And now there's no one left to protect.

00:29:38.384 --> 00:29:39.751
Yes, there is.

00:29:49.018 --> 00:29:51.117
Oh, my life was so simple.

00:29:51.150 --> 00:29:55.617
Just school, exams,

00:29:55.651 --> 00:29:59.150
Papers on polycentric cultural norms.

00:29:59.183 --> 00:30:03.083
So i guess i saved you
from a boring existence.

00:30:03.117 --> 00:30:05.284
Occasionally i miss boring.

00:30:07.050 --> 00:30:08.617
So, this killer truck...

00:30:08.651 --> 00:30:12.517
I miss conversations that didn't
start with "this killer truck."

00:30:12.551 --> 00:30:14.984
Ah...

00:30:15.018 --> 00:30:16.951
All right, well, this cyrus guy,

00:30:16.984 --> 00:30:19.617
Evil on a level that
infected even his truck.

00:30:19.651 --> 00:30:23.150
When he died, the swamp became his tomb

00:30:23.183 --> 00:30:25.517
And his spirit was dormant for 40 years.

00:30:25.551 --> 00:30:26.751
So, what woke it up?

00:30:26.784 --> 00:30:29.350
The construction on his
house or the destructi.

00:30:29.384 --> 00:30:30.484
Right.

00:30:30.517 --> 00:30:33.284
Demolition or remodeling
can awaken spirits,

00:30:33.317 --> 00:30:35.018
Make them restless.

00:30:35.050 --> 00:30:37.417
Like that theater in illinois.

00:30:37.450 --> 00:30:38.684
Yeah.

00:30:38.717 --> 00:30:40.717
And the guy who tears
down the family homestead,

00:30:40.751 --> 00:30:43.250
Harold todd, is the same guy

00:30:43.284 --> 00:30:46.817
That kept cyrus's murder
quiet and unsolved.

00:30:46.851 --> 00:30:49.018
So now his spirit is
awakened and out for blood.

00:30:49.050 --> 00:30:51.317
I guess. Who knows what
ghosts are thinking anyway.

00:30:51.350 --> 00:30:54.717
You know we're gonna have to
dredge that body from the swamp?

00:30:54.751 --> 00:30:56.350
Maman.

00:30:56.384 --> 00:30:58.717
You said it. Yeah.

00:30:58.751 --> 00:30:59.717
Hey.

00:30:59.751 --> 00:31:00.717
Hey.

00:31:00.751 --> 00:31:02.784
She's asleep.

00:31:02.817 --> 00:31:04.884
Now what?

00:31:04.918 --> 00:31:06.617
You stay put and look after her.

00:31:06.651 --> 00:31:08.717
And we'll be back.
Don't leave the house.

00:31:08.751 --> 00:31:10.951
Don't go getting all
authoritative on me.

00:31:10.984 --> 00:31:12.050
I hate it.

00:31:13.484 --> 00:31:16.217
Don't leave the house, please?

00:31:28.183 --> 00:31:30.918
You coming or what?

00:31:35.517 --> 00:31:39.117
Sam: All right, let's get her up.

00:31:40.684 --> 00:31:43.918
All right. Little more.

00:31:43.951 --> 00:31:45.183
Little more.

00:31:46.450 --> 00:31:48.651
Litt more.

00:31:48.684 --> 00:31:49.918
All right, stop.

00:31:58.551 --> 00:31:59.684
Nice.

00:31:59.717 --> 00:32:01.784
Hell yeah.

00:32:01.817 --> 00:32:03.183
Now i know what she sees in you.

00:32:03.217 --> 00:32:04.450
What?

00:32:04.484 --> 00:32:07.018
Come on, you can admit it.
You're still in love with her.

00:32:07.050 --> 00:32:08.317
Can we focus, please?

00:32:08.350 --> 00:32:10.183
I'm just saying, dean.

00:32:10.217 --> 00:32:11.217
Hold that.

00:32:11.250 --> 00:32:13.851
All right. What am i getting?

00:32:13.884 --> 00:32:15.450
Gas, flashlight. Got it, got it.

00:32:15.484 --> 00:32:16.984
All right, let's get this done.

00:32:17.018 --> 00:32:19.250
All right. Got it.

00:32:36.551 --> 00:32:38.083
All right, let's get to it.

00:32:53.651 --> 00:32:56.250
Think that'll do it?

00:33:02.083 --> 00:33:04.050
I guess not.

00:33:07.677 --> 00:33:09.577
So burning the body had
no effect on that thing?

00:33:09.610 --> 00:33:10.944
Sure it did. Now it's really pissed.

00:33:10.977 --> 00:33:12.910
But cyrus's ghost is gone, right, dean?

00:33:12.944 --> 00:33:14.710
Apparently not the part
that's fused with the truck.

00:33:14.984 --> 00:33:16.783
Where you going?

00:33:16.817 --> 00:33:19.184
Going for a little ride.
Gonna lead that thing away.

00:33:19.217 --> 00:33:21.017
That rusted piece of
crap, you got to burn it.

00:33:21.050 --> 00:33:22.651
How the hell am i supposed
to burn a truck, dean?

00:33:22.684 --> 00:33:24.517
I don't know. Figure something out.

00:33:24.891 --> 00:33:26.524
Figure something...

00:34:06.421 --> 00:34:08.588
Hey, you got to give me a minute.

00:34:08.620 --> 00:34:10.121
I don't have a minute!
What are we doing?!

00:34:10.154 --> 00:34:13.121
Uh... let me get back to you.

00:34:15.588 --> 00:34:17.121
Hey, cassie? Hey, it's sam.

00:34:17.154 --> 00:34:20.187
Okay, i need some information
and it has to be exactly right.

00:34:23.454 --> 00:34:25.154
All right, dean. This better be good!

00:34:25.187 --> 00:34:28.787
Where are you? I'm in the middle of
nowhere with a killer truck on my ass!

00:34:28.820 --> 00:34:31.020
It's like it knows i
put the torch to cyrus!

00:34:31.054 --> 00:34:32.720
Dean, listen to me. It's important.

00:34:32.753 --> 00:34:33.820
I have to know exactly where you are.

00:34:33.854 --> 00:34:36.254
Decatur road, about two
miles off the highway.

00:34:36.287 --> 00:34:38.054
Okay, headed east? Yes!

00:34:42.987 --> 00:34:46.187
Oh, you son of a bitch.

00:34:46.221 --> 00:34:47.454
Okay, uh, turn right.

00:34:54.454 --> 00:34:55.653
You make the turn?

00:34:55.687 --> 00:34:57.087
Yeah, i made the turn!

00:34:57.121 --> 00:34:58.854
Move this thing along a little faster!

00:34:58.887 --> 00:35:00.454
All right, you see a road up ahead?

00:35:00.488 --> 00:35:01.687
No!

00:35:01.720 --> 00:35:03.454
Wait, yes, i see it!

00:35:03.488 --> 00:35:05.087
Okay, turn left. What?!

00:35:12.588 --> 00:35:14.154
All right, now what?

00:35:14.187 --> 00:35:16.154
Go exactly 7/10ths of a mile and stop.

00:35:16.187 --> 00:35:18.854
Stop? Exactly 7/10ths, dean.

00:35:18.887 --> 00:35:21.254
7/10ths, 7/10ths.

00:35:50.720 --> 00:35:53.554
Dean, are you still there?

00:35:53.588 --> 00:35:55.254
Yeah. What's happening?

00:35:55.287 --> 00:35:57.254
It's just staring at me. What do i do?

00:35:57.287 --> 00:35:59.653
Just what you are doing...
bringing it to you.

00:35:59.687 --> 00:36:00.753
Wh...

00:36:17.820 --> 00:36:19.354
Come on, come on.

00:36:39.387 --> 00:36:42.054
Dean?

00:36:42.087 --> 00:36:43.287
You still there?

00:36:43.321 --> 00:36:46.154
Dean?

00:36:46.187 --> 00:36:48.588
Where'd it go?

00:36:48.620 --> 00:36:51.820
Dean, you're where the church was.

00:36:51.854 --> 00:36:53.087
What church?

00:36:53.121 --> 00:36:55.588
The place cyrus burned down
and murdered all those kids.

00:36:55.620 --> 00:36:57.221
There's not a whole lot left.

00:36:57.254 --> 00:36:58.954
Church ground is hallowed ground

00:36:58.987 --> 00:37:00.488
Whether the church
is still there or not.

00:37:00.521 --> 00:37:02.554
Evil spirits cross over hallowed ground,

00:37:02.588 --> 00:37:04.321
Sometimes they're destroyed.

00:37:04.354 --> 00:37:09.254
So i figured maybe that
would get rid of it.

00:37:09.287 --> 00:37:10.287
Maybe?

00:37:10.321 --> 00:37:11.620
Maybe?!

00:37:11.653 --> 00:37:14.354
What if you were wrong?!

00:37:16.121 --> 00:37:18.820
Honestly, that thought
hadn't occurred to me.

00:37:23.020 --> 00:37:25.321
"Well, that honestly
didn't occur to me."

00:37:31.321 --> 00:37:32.987
I'm gonna kill him.

00:37:39.974 --> 00:37:43.007
My mother says to tell you thanks again.

00:37:47.940 --> 00:37:50.841
This was a better goodbye
than the last time.

00:37:50.874 --> 00:37:52.808
Yeah, well, maybe this time

00:37:52.841 --> 00:37:55.107
It'll be a little less permanent.

00:37:55.140 --> 00:37:58.707
You know what?

00:37:58.741 --> 00:38:01.741
I'm a realist.

00:38:01.774 --> 00:38:04.707
I don't see much hope for us, dean.

00:38:08.374 --> 00:38:11.240
Well, i've seen stranger things happen.

00:38:11.274 --> 00:38:12.940
Hell of a lot stranger.

00:38:17.607 --> 00:38:19.474
Goodbye, dean.

00:38:19.507 --> 00:38:22.474
I'll see you, cassie.

00:38:22.507 --> 00:38:25.441
I will.

00:39:18.007 --> 00:39:20.107
I like her.

00:39:20.140 --> 00:39:21.474
Yeah.

00:39:23.808 --> 00:39:25.574
You meet someone like her,

00:39:25.607 --> 00:39:28.407
Ever make you wonder if it's worth it...

00:39:28.441 --> 00:39:32.541
Putting everything else
on hold, doing what we do?

00:39:45.107 --> 00:39:48.207
Why don't you wake me up
when it's my turn to drive?



00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.000
